-- title:
--   Equal principal ideals in T[[X]] force a unit multiple
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring that is local and Noetherian, let $\iota$ be a type, let $S$ be a finite subset of $\iota$ and let $z : \iota \to T$ be a family of elements with $z_i$ in the maximal ideal of $T$ for every $i \in S$. Write $p = \prod_{i \in S} (X - C(z_i))$ for the corresponding product in the power series ring $T[\![X]\!]$, where $C$ denotes the constant-coefficient inclusion $T \to T[\![X]\!]$. Let $x \in T[\![X]\!]$ and assume that the principal ideals generated by $x$ and by $p$ coincide, i.e. $\mathrm{span}\{x\} = \mathrm{span}\{p\}$ as ideals of $T[\![X]\!]$. Then there exists $u \in T[\![X]\!]$ which is a unit and satisfies $u \cdot x = p$. Thus $x$ and $\prod_{i \in S}(X - C(z_i))$ differ by a unit of $T[\![X]\!]$; no hypothesis of injectivity on $z$ or of distinctness of the $z_i$ is required, and $S$ may be empty, in which case $p = 1$.
--
--   Generators of equal principal ideals are associates whenever the generator in question is a non-zero-divisor; here that non-zero-divisor property is established for products of linear factors $X - C(z_i)$ with $z_i$ in the maximal ideal of a local Noetherian ring. The result is used in the Drinfeld-basis material on Weierstrass models, where the power series cutting out a divisor supported at prescribed torsion parameters near the origin must be normalised to the explicit product of linear factors.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PowerSeries_exists_isUnit_mul_eq_prod_X_sub_C_of_span_eq.lean

